<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46429" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sufflāmen</span></b> ,
		ĭnis, n.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				clog</i>, <i>break</i>, <i>drag-chain</i>, to check the motion of a wheel. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rotam astringit multo sufflamine,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					8, 148</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tardat sufflamine currum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Psych. 417</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>a clog</i>, <i>hinderance</i>, <i>impediment</i>
			(post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nec res atteritur longo sufflamine litis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					16, 50</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 180, 3</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
